><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250516124742+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250516124744+10'00'" name="f26d8616-faa8-4657-b6eb-49c38a73443b" page="6" coords="53.801071,343.258698,284.246155,343.258698,53.801071,333.463409,284.246155,333.463409,41.838593,332.770721,284.187805,332.770721,41.838593,322.975433,284.187805,322.975433,41.838608,322.339325,284.173523,322.339325,41.838608,312.544037,284.173523,312.544037,41.838608,311.851349,284.164978,311.851349,41.838608,302.056061,284.164978,302.056061,41.838608,301.419952,284.208740,301.419952,41.838608,291.624664,284.208740,291.624664,41.838608,290.931976,284.206207,290.931976,41.838608,281.136688,284.206207,281.136688,41.838593,280.500580,284.159485,280.500580,41.838593,270.705292,284.159485,270.705292,41.838593,270.012604,284.200134,270.012604,41.838593,260.217316,284.200134,260.217316,41.838593,259.581207,284.261841,259.581207,41.838593,249.785919,284.261841,249.785919,41.837799,249.093231,284.203857,249.093231,41.837799,239.297943,284.203857,239.297943,41.837799,238.661835,284.164490,238.661835,41.837799,228.866547,284.164490,228.866547,41.837784,228.173828,204.451691,228.173828,41.837784,218.378540,204.451691,218.378540" rect="41.531677,218.072433,284.567932,343.564819" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The results of the present study demonstrated that PP juice&#xD;intake with a high-fat/CHO muffin potentially decreased autonomic&#xD;cardiac regulation (HRV) and did not improve the traditional CVD&#xD;risk blood biomarker responses such as TC or BP. The study results&#xD;suggested the negative effects of high CHO intake on acute HRV&#xD;responses up to 3 h post-consumption. The significant effects are&#xD;attributed to the differences in composition between trial foods and&#xD;highlight the need to consider the CHO levels of fruit in study&#xD;designs when attempting to understand the health benefits of bioactives,&#xD;such as betalains. Nonetheless, the consumption of PP fruit&#xD;juice may increase awareness of its putative health benefits and&#xD;may promote consumption of the whole fruit.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="yes" page="6" rect="575.998718,55.168640,759.925598,343.168030"
/></highlight
